{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the Valley of Siddim was full of bitumen pits.</b> Our Rabbis interpreted that these were pits containing much clay, from which people would take earth for building; and a miracle was performed for the king of Sodom so that he escaped, for there were some among the nations who did not believe that Abraham had been saved from the fiery furnace, and once this one emerged from the bitumen, they believed in Abraham retroactively." "<b>And the Ramban, of blessed memory, wrote</b> — and one should wonder: for surely the nations who did not believe in the miracle of Abraham in the fiery furnace, upon seeing the miracle of the king of Sodom, would not thereby increase their faith in the Holy One, blessed be He. Rather, the miracle of the king of Sodom would strengthen the hands of idol worshippers, for the king of Sodom was an idol worshipper; and even to believers, the miracle of Abraham our father would plant doubt in them." "<b>Rather,</b> the explanation of this Midrash is that the king of Sodom was saved in the merit of Abraham, and a miracle was performed for him so that he emerged to greet Abraham, to honor him and to bless him; and Abraham, upon his return, looked at that pit, for he sought to rescue the kings and restore their property to them. And so the intent of the Sages is: if a miracle was performed for the king of Sodom for the honor of Abraham, how much more so should one believe that a miracle would be performed for Abraham himself, to save him from the fiery furnace. End." "<b>And in the Midrash:</b> 'And the Valley of Siddim' — which nursed them like a wet-nurse (שדים) for an infant. This is the Dead (Salt) Sea, in whose punishment that valley became salty waters; as it is said (Psalms 107): ארץ פרי למלחה מרעת יושבי בה."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:12:20.833885615Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}